{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And after that</b> — after the festival of Sukkot. Burnt offerings that are continual, in place of the four, and so it is the continual burnt offering which was not discontinued, and the burnt offering of the new months, and the burnt offering for every appointed time of HaShem." "<b>The consecrated things</b> — those called holy by decree of the court, and a burnt offering for every volunteer. And the reason is that the offerings were not discontinued after that, from the beginning of Tishrei, for they had begun to offer burnt offerings."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:54.893282405Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}